# Always close a session by asking "what's next?"

When you finish the work you were asked to do, **do not end the turn with only
a summary**. Use the `AskQuestion` tool to offer concrete, ranked next steps so
the user can choose without typing a fresh brief.

## How to do it

- Ask **after** the work is done and verified, as the last thing in the turn.
- Offer **real candidates drawn from this repo's own queues**, not generic
  filler. The live sources are:
  - [ROADMAP.md](../../ROADMAP.md) — ranked candidate games.
  - `docs/GAME-DESIGNS-*.md` — the approved design set and its build order.
  - `CONTEXT.md` §7 "Current state & what's next" — open follow-ups and debts.
- Put the option you'd recommend **first** and mark it `(Recommended)`.
- Include open debt/bugs as options when they compete with new features, and
  say plainly which one is actually user-facing.

## Example

After shipping a game, ask something like:

- "Build Opposites Friends (next in the arc, prereq fixed) **(Recommended)**"
- "Fix dark mode across the 11 StoryLayout themes — broken for users today"
- "Migrate the 23 shake-only games to the red + error-tone feedback rule"

## Don't

- Don't ask mid-task, and don't ask instead of finishing the work.
- Don't list the options as prose bullets in the reply — use `AskQuestion`, so
  the choices are selectable.
